{"t":{"t":10,"i":0,"p":{"k":["result","context"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":1,"p":{"k":["type","title","description","props"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"openapi"},{"t":1,"s":"Explain one of the caller's offers in plain language"},{"t":1,"s":"Numbers come from the stored quote; model text is checked against them before it is shown."},{"t":10,"i":2,"p":{"k":["payload","document","operations","showDescription"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":3,"p":{"k":["bundled","proxyUrl"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":4,"p":{"k":["openapi","info","servers","tags","paths","components"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"3.2.0"},{"t":10,"i":5,"p":{"k":["title","version","summary","description","license","contact"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"GridWindow FlexPay API"},{"t":1,"s":"1.0.0"},{"t":1,"s":"Consented flexible overnight EV charging, settled with PayPal (authorize, then capture or void from delivered energy)."},{"t":1,"s":"The public driver API behind GridWindow FlexPay, plus the operator endpoints.\\n\\n**Flow.** A driver (or an AI agent acting for one, see `docs/MCP.md`) reads the site, requests priced offers,\\noptionally asks the deal agent for a pick, then accepts one exact offer. Accepting creates a PayPal Orders v2\\n**AUTHORIZE** order and returns an `approveUrl`; only the human buyer can approve it in PayPal. The server then\\nauthorizes, commits the charging slots, and later captures for delivered energy or voids. The client never sets a price\\nand never moves money.\\n\\n**Sessions.** Driver identity is a signed `gw_drv` cookie created on the first quote. Operator endpoints need the\\n`gw_op` cookie from `POST /api/operator/session`. Mutating requests must come from an allowed origin (`Origin` header).\\n\\n**Money.** All amounts are integer US cents. Payments are PayPal **Sandbox** (test money) or a labelled MOCK provider.\\n"},{"t":10,"i":6,"p":{"k":["name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"See LICENSE"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":7,"p":{"k":["name","url"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"GridWindow FlexPay team"},{"t":1,"s":"https://github.com/piyusha-sayal/gridwindow-flexpay"